## Initialize the cluster
First, identify the private IP:

hostname -I
Suppose the private IP is:
172.31.10.10

Run:
sudo kubeadm init \
--apiserver-advertise-address=172.31.10.10 \
--pod-network-cidr=10.244.0.0/16

Replace the IP with your Master private IP.

What happens internally when we execute kubeadm init?
Kubeadm performs several operations:
1. Performs preflight checks.
2. Generates Kubernetes certificates.
3. Generates kubeconfig files.
4. Creates etcd static Pod manifest.
5. Creates API Server static Pod manifest.
6. Creates Controller Manager static Pod manifest.
7. Creates Scheduler static Pod manifest.
8. Configures kubelet.
9. Starts the Control Plane components.
10. Creates bootstrap tokens.
11. Configures CoreDNS.
12. Configures kube-proxy.

Official documentation explains the complete initialization process and its phases. Kubernetes
